  ApiEndpoint(
    method: 'POST',
    path: '/api/v0/storage/devices/snapshot-backup',
    inSwagger: true,
    tags: ['storage'],
    summary: 'Start a snapshot backup to a device',
    description: 'Queues a job that copies the data drives onto the target snapshot-backup device. sourceSerials names the data drives to copy; empty or absent is every data drive, every managed device but the target and the other snapshot-backup drives. Built-in storage is the serial "", as it is for targetDeviceSerial. Each named serial must be an attached data drive; the target, another snapshot-backup drive, or a drive that is not attached is a 400. The job name and the run name only the drives copied. Answers 409 while the target already has a pending or running backup, whichever instance started it, and 409 when the target\'s health.verdict is replace-soon unless acknowledgeHealth is true. Watch does not block. It asks for no password. On SQLite the snapshot also copies the chat and every account\'s vault, as the ciphertext they are, into chat_backup.db and vault_items_backup.db. On PostgreSQL the snapshot is the device directories and backup_manifest.json only: the chat and the vault are in the operator\'s database backup.\nEach backup is a new run in its own folder under backups/, named for the minute it started in the Quark\'s local time, as "2026-11-07 21.57", with " (2)" and so on when two start in the same minute. A run holds one folder per source drive ("Built-in storage", or the drive\'s name and the first 8 characters of its serial, as "Photos (USB 90C82C65)"), the chat and vault files, and the manifest, which records each drive folder\'s source serial.\nA run is written under a hidden folder ending in .partial and renamed when it completes; a failed or canceled run\'s partial folder is removed. A file unchanged since the newest complete run holding its drive is hard-linked from it where the drive\'s filesystem allows, and copied otherwise. No source\'s own backups/ folder is copied. The backup never deletes a file. jobId is what the status route takes.\nBefore copying, the backup compares the drive\'s free space with the bytes the run will copy, every file it cannot hard-link. While that is short it deletes the oldest complete run, one at a time, and publishes backup_deleted for each; it never deletes the newest complete run, nor the newest run holding any drive (a drive\'s newest copy), nor a run a restore is reading. If the drive is still short, the backup fails before copying with a message naming the drive, such as "not enough space on Backup for this backup: delete old backups or use a bigger drive". A drive whose free space cannot be read is not pruned.',
    parameters: [
      ApiParameter(
        name: 'body',
        location: ApiParameterLocation.body,
        required: true,
        type: 'object',
        description: '{targetDeviceSerial: string, sourceSerials: []string, acknowledgeHealth: bool}',
      ),
    ],
    requestSchema: '{"type":"object"}',
    responses: [
      ApiResponse(
        status: '202',
        description: 'Accepted',
        schema: '{"type":"object"}',
      ),
      ApiResponse(
        status: '400',
        description: 'target without the role or not attached, or a source that is not an attached data drive',
        schema: '{"type":"object","properties":{"contentType":{"type":"string","enum":["text/html","application/json"],"x-enum-varnames":["ContentTypeHTML","ContentTypeJSON"]},"data":{},"error":{},"statusCode":{"type":"integer"}}}',
      ),
      ApiResponse(
        status: '409',
        description: 'backup already running, or a replace-soon target was not acknowledged',
        schema: '{"type":"object","properties":{"contentType":{"type":"string","enum":["text/html","application/json"],"x-enum-varnames":["ContentTypeHTML","ContentTypeJSON"]},"data":{},"error":{},"statusCode":{"type":"integer"}}}',
      ),
      ApiResponse(
        status: '500',
        description: 'Internal Server Error',
        schema: '{"type":"object","properties":{"contentType":{"type":"string","enum":["text/html","application/json"],"x-enum-varnames":["ContentTypeHTML","ContentTypeJSON"]},"data":{},"error":{},"statusCode":{"type":"integer"}}}',
      ),
    ],
    callers: ['StorageService.startSnapshotBackup'],
  ),
  ApiEndpoint(
    method: 'POST',
    path: '/api/v0/storage/devices/snapshot-backup/restore-chat',
    inSwagger: true,
    tags: ['storage'],
    summary: 'Restore the chat from a snapshot backup',
    description: 'Re-confirms the caller with password, which carries the auth key of the admin\'s login password, exactly as POST /storage/devices/snapshot-backup/restore-vault takes it; a wrong or missing key is a 403, a raw password is a 426, and nothing is restored. Shares the sign-in rate limit, and the body is at most 1 KiB.\nThen restores the chat backup a snapshot wrote into one run on the drive, which must have the snapshot-backup role: run, a folder under backups/, or the newest complete run when it is empty. The answer names the run.\nThe restore replaces an empty chat: one with no message and no channel but general. A chat that already has messages or channels is refused, and a refused or failed restore changes nothing.\nThe backup does not carry accounts. Every account it names is matched by username on this Quark; unmatchedUsers names the ones that are not here, whose messages stay with no author and whose memberships, reactions and chat keys are not restored.\nAlso refused, changing nothing, when this Quark did not write the backup: its MAC is another Quark\'s, the file changed after the snapshot, or its MAC is gone from a drive this Quark binds its snapshots to. A snapshot taken before binding still restores.\nEvery channel\'s members are sent chat_channel_changed. Every attempt past the password check is written to the server log.',
    parameters: [
      ApiParameter(
        name: 'body',
        location: ApiParameterLocation.body,
        required: true,
        type: 'object',
        description: 'The backup drive, the run, and the admin\'s auth key',
      ),
    ],
    requestSchema: '{"type":"object","properties":{"deviceSerial":{"description":"\\"\\" is built-in storage, so the field is not binding:\\"required\\".","type":"string"},"password":{"description":"Password is the standard base64 auth key of the admin\'s login\\npassword, as DELETE /vault takes it.","type":"string"},"run":{"description":"Run is the run to restore from, a folder under backups/ on the drive.\\nEmpty is the newest complete run.","type":"string"}}}',
    responses: [
      ApiResponse(
        status: '200',
        description: 'OK',
        schema: '{"type":"object","properties":{"channels":{"type":"integer"},"messages":{"type":"integer"},"run":{"description":"Run is the run [RestoreChat] read the chat from, a folder under\\nbackups/. [ImportChat] leaves it empty.","type":"string"},"unmatchedUsers":{"description":"UnmatchedUsers is the usernames in the backup with no account on this\\nQuark, sorted. Their messages read as a deleted account\'s, and their\\nmemberships, reactions and chat keys were not restored.","type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}}}',
